== cd into a directory colors it as a valid path:
cd	\e[1m
adir	\e[96m
== cd into a file colors it red:
cd	\e[1m
afile	\e[4:3;58:5:1m
== ls of the same file stays a valid path:
ls	\e[1m
afile	\e[96m
== a trailing separator rejects a file:
./afile/	\e[4:3;58:5:1m
== a trailing separator rejects a symlink to a file:
./alink/	\e[4:3;58:5:1m
== a trailing separator accepts a directory:
